Store all column properties in 1 column.

Example: if two columns namespace and cluster have URLs defined, the attributes columns will store their url

```json
{
  "namespace": {
    "url": "/view/xx/yy"
  },
  "cluster": {
    "url": "/view/monitoring/beta"
  }
}
```

As we add new properties (eg: gauge.max value)

```json
{
  "namespace": {
    "url": "/view/xx/yy"
  },
  "cpu": {
    "gauge": {
      "max": 1000
    }
  },
  "cluster": {
    "url": "/view/monitoring/beta"
  }
}

```

This PR addresses critical UI functionality issues and implements a professional-grade audio trimming system for the DYHT Audio DVR Dashboard.

## Issues Fixed

### 1. Non-functional Trim Button
The trim button previously only showed a placeholder alert. Now it opens a fully-featured audio trimming interface with:
- Visual timeline with precise start/end markers
- Real-time audio processing and WAV file generation
- Slider and numeric controls for exact timing
- Audio playback and navigation tools
- Mock audio generation for testing without microphone access

### 2. Dwight Panel Growth Breaking UI Layout
The Dwight AI chat panel could grow indefinitely, making trigger controls inaccessible. Fixed by:
- Adding `maxHeight: 500px` constraint to the main panel
- Limiting message area to `maxHeight: 300px` with proper scrolling
- Maintaining full accessibility to all trigger panel controls

### 3. Missing Privacy Controls
Added a prominent emergency kill switch that:
- Instantly disables all recording, AI chat, and listening functions
- Provides clear visual feedback with red styling throughout the UI
- Includes privacy mode messaging and easy restoration
- Ensures user privacy with one-click system shutdown

## Technical Implementation

### Audio Trimming System
```typescript
// Professional audio processing with AudioContext
const trimAudio = async () => {
  const trimmedBuffer = audioContext.createBuffer(channels, length, sampleRate);
  // Copy selected portion with sample-accurate precision
  for (let channel = 0; channel < channels; channel++) {
    const sourceData = sourceBuffer.getChannelData(channel);
    const trimmedData = trimmedBuffer.getChannelData(channel);
    for (let i = 0; i < trimmedLength; i++) {
      trimmedData[i] = sourceData[startSample + i];
    }
  }
};
```

### UI Layout Constraints
```typescript
// Prevent excessive panel growth while maintaining functionality
<div style={{
  maxHeight: "500px", // Main panel constraint
  // ...other styles
}}>
  <div style={{
    maxHeight: "300px", // Message area scrolling
    overflowY: "auto"
  }}>
```

### Kill Switch Implementation
```typescript
const handleKillSwitch = () => {
  if (!isKillSwitchActive) {
    audioRecorder.stopRecording();
    stopDwightSpeaking();
    setTranscript([{ type: "speech", text: "🔴 PRIVACY MODE ACTIVATED" }]);
  }
};
```

## User Experience Improvements

- **Audio Trimming**: Professional interface with visual feedback and precise controls
- **Privacy Protection**: One-click emergency disable for all system functions  
- **Layout Stability**: Panels maintain proper sizing regardless of content
- **Visual Feedback**: Clear status indicators and smooth transitions
- **Accessibility**: All controls remain reachable under all conditions

## Testing

The implementation includes comprehensive testing features:
- Mock audio generation (10-second 440Hz test tone)
- Real-time trim preview and validation
- Complete state management and cleanup
- Error handling with user-friendly messages

All features have been verified to work correctly, maintaining backward compatibility while significantly enhancing functionality and user safety.

